{{Quote|Mandalore's violent past is behind us. All of our warriors were exiled to our moon, Concordia. They died out years ago.|An incorrect Prime Minister Almec|<ref name="The Mandalore Plot" />}}
'''Mandalorian warriors''', also known as '''Mandalorian commandos''', were [[soldier]]s of [[Mandalorian]] [[Mandalorian clan|clans]] that were active throughout Mandalorian cultural history. Many Mandalorian warriors were part of Mandalorian organizations such as [[Death Watch]], [[Journeyman Protector|Mandalorian Protectors]], [[Nite Owls]], and the [[Children of the Watch]]. Overall, Mandalorians served as soldiers, [[assassin]]s, [[bounty hunter]]s, [[Mercenary|mercenaries]], and [[saboteur]]s.

==Description==
[[Mandalorian]] [[Soldier|warriors]],<ref name="Sabine DB" /> also referred to as Mandalorian commandos,<ref name="Pre Vizsla DB">{{Databank|pre-vizsla|Pre Vizsla}}</ref> were Mandalorian soldiers that embodied [[Mandalore]]'s warrior heritage and served warrior-centric [[Mandalorian clan]]s.<ref name="Death Watch DB" /> They used various types of [[Mandalorian armor]], including [[Mandalorian rally master armor]]. Mandalorian warriors used the [[military rank]] of [[rally master]],<ref name="Solo TG">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]''</ref> and the group [[Death Watch]] used a [[Rank insignia (Death Watch)|rank insignia]].<ref name="Mandalore Plot Concept">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-mandalore-plot-concept-art-gallery|text="The Mandalore Plot" Concept Art Gallery}} {{C|Slide 11}}</ref> [[Jaig Eyes]] were a combat honor that adorned<ref name="Updated and Expanded">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> the [[helmet]]s of Mandalorian warriors.<ref name="Collapse" />

==History==
After the [[Great Clan Wars]], the [[New Mandalorians]] led by [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]] adopted and created a pacifist society, a sharp turn from Mandalore's warrior culture. Those who did not accept were exiled to Concordia, and by the [[time]] of the [[Clone Wars]] were thought to have died out. In reality, however, warriors were still active and grouped into the organization known as Death Watch, which was secretly led by [[Pre Vizsla]]. The Mandalorian [[bounty hunter]] and [[foundling]] [[Jango Fett]], who participated in the [[Mandalorian Civil Wars]], was a famous individual who wore a [[Boba Fett's armor|distinctive set of Mandalorian armor]], although the New Mandalorian government did not know how he obtained it.<ref name="The Mandalore Plot" /> Death Watch was active throughout the [[Cloning|Clone]] Wars, eventually joining the [[Shadow Collective]] led by [[Maul]] and overthrew the New Mandalorian government and [[Mandalorian Civil War (19 BBY)|civil war]] erupted once again.<ref name="The Lawless" />

After the rise of the [[Galactic Empire]], [[Imperial Super Commando]]s were formed and served the Empire,<ref name="Imperial Super Commandos">{{Rebels|Imperial Supercommandos}}</ref> while other Mandalorian warriors were active in their respective clans. The [[Journeyman Protector|Mandalorian Protectors]] remained active in the [[Concord Dawn system]].<ref name="Protectors">{{Rebels|The Protector of Concord Dawn}}</ref> After the [[Great Purge of Mandalore]] against the Mandalorians and the fall of the Empire, at least one group of Mandalorian warriors known as [[the Tribe]] operated in secrecy.<ref name="Chapter 1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref> When [[Din Djarin]] was granted his own [[signet]]&mdash;establishing [[Clan Mudhorn]] in the process&mdash;and a [[jetpack]] by "[[the Armorer]]" during the [[Clash on Nevarro]],<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref> the act acknowledged that he was a full Mandalorian warrior.<ref name="Journey">{{InsiderCite|216|The Journey of Din Djarin}}</ref>

